<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iestyn ap Gwrgant</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iestyn ap Gwrgant was the last native king of Morgannwg, or Glamorgan, in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> in the late 11th century. Around 1090 he was overthrown by the Norman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-fitzhamon">Robert Fitzhamon</a>, who built a castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardiff">Cardiff</a> and created the marcher Lordship of Glamorgan. Later Welsh tradition blamed Iestyn for inviting the Normans in, and several Glamorgan families claimed descent from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iestyn-ap-gwrgant.jpg" alt="Iestyn ap Gwrgant" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AlexD · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_morgannwg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
